            <div xml:id="d147">

                <pb facs="0222" n="146" sameAs="frus:frus1916/pg146"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 893.51/1716</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        Minister Reinsch
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-12-05">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">December 5, 1916</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Department’s telegram December 4. You are authorized to take occasion to intimate
                    to your colleagues representing Governments of group bankers’ nationalities that
                    any strained construction of existing agreements between the Chinese Government
                    and bankers, or any attempt to exclude our bankers from a fair participation in
                    Chinese affairs, would meet with very decided resistance from this
                    Government.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
